    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287-a1">

                <pb facs="0406" n="318" xml:id="pg318"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Brittain to Mr. Dodge.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Consulate</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Kehl</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1903-12-18"><hi
                                rendition="#italic">December 18,
                    1903</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg to inclose the citizenship papers of
                    Emil Vibert, who wishes to return to Germany for the purpose of a visit.</p>
                <p>He would like to have permission to visit his old home for a period of six
                    months, namely from April 1 until September 30, 1904.</p>
                <p>Mr. Vibert went to the United States with his father in 1886, at the age of 12
                    years. His father resides now at St. Quirin, Lorraine, near Saarburg.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Joseph I.
                    Brittain.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
